00:34:14.760 --> 00:34:16.260
JON FOUST: That
question of the week

00:34:16.260 --> 00:34:19.335
was, when I SSH in my VM
via different methods,

00:34:19.335 --> 00:34:20.460
I get a different username.

00:34:20.460 --> 00:34:22.790
So what can I do to
make that static?

00:34:22.790 --> 00:34:24.540
BRIAN DORSEY: That can
be super confusing.

00:34:24.540 --> 00:34:26.412
Because if you're, by default--

00:34:26.412 --> 00:34:28.620
and this is talking about
SSH-ing into Compute Engine

00:34:28.620 --> 00:34:32.130
instances-- the user
name is kind of just

00:34:32.130 --> 00:34:36.150
passed through from what
your host environment is.

00:34:36.150 --> 00:34:37.949
So if you're on
the Cloud console,

00:34:37.949 --> 00:34:40.590
that's going to be the first
part of your email address

00:34:40.590 --> 00:34:43.110
of whatever you're log
in to Google Cloud is.

00:34:43.110 --> 00:34:46.133
Then, if you, later, go and
SSH in from your laptop,

00:34:46.133 --> 00:34:48.300
you might have a different
user name on your laptop.

00:34:48.300 --> 00:34:50.100
And then you're logging
into the same machine,

00:34:50.100 --> 00:34:51.449
but you end up with
two different user

00:34:51.449 --> 00:34:52.350
accounts on that end.

00:34:52.350 --> 00:34:54.528
And your dot files
don't work the same way,

00:34:54.528 --> 00:34:56.320
or the permissions
don't work the same way,

00:34:56.320 --> 00:34:57.880
and it gets all confusing.

00:34:57.880 --> 00:34:59.890
So there's a couple of options.

00:34:59.890 --> 00:35:02.760
One is that you could
change all of things.

00:35:02.760 --> 00:35:04.710
Now that's not so super useful.

00:35:04.710 --> 00:35:07.140
When you SSH in
from your laptop--

00:35:07.140 --> 00:35:09.420
and this is a feature that
might not be that known,

00:35:09.420 --> 00:35:10.930
so just to talk about it a bit.

00:35:10.930 --> 00:35:14.670
As part of gcloud, there's a
gcloud compute ssh, and then

00:35:14.670 --> 00:35:15.660
an instance name.

00:35:15.660 --> 00:35:20.040
And since you're already logged
in with OAuth to Google Cloud,

00:35:20.040 --> 00:35:22.770
it handles the SSH key pair
exchange and all that sort

00:35:22.770 --> 00:35:23.478
of stuff for you.

00:35:23.478 --> 00:35:25.145
And it just does all
the configurations,

00:35:25.145 --> 00:35:26.710
so you don't have
to worry about it.

00:35:26.710 --> 00:35:28.410
But one of the things it
does in that automatic thing

00:35:28.410 --> 00:35:30.102
is figure out what user to use.

00:35:30.102 --> 00:35:31.810
And it just infers
that from your laptop.

00:35:31.810 --> 00:35:36.168
So the fix is, actually, really
simple but hard to notice.

00:35:36.168 --> 00:35:38.460
So it's great if you know
it's there, not if you don't.

00:35:38.460 --> 00:35:40.650
And it's, basically,
you just add,

00:35:40.650 --> 00:35:44.100
instead of just the instance
name, user@ the instance name.

00:35:44.100 --> 00:35:47.850
And then that will set the
remote user to log into.

00:35:47.850 --> 00:35:49.470
And you're good to go.

00:35:49.470 --> 00:35:53.340
So gcloud compute
SSH, user@ instance.

00:35:53.340 --> 00:35:54.373
And that will work.

00:35:54.373 --> 00:35:55.540
So that's the short version.

00:35:55.540 --> 00:35:59.760
There is a more, kind of
managed version of SSH keys

00:35:59.760 --> 00:36:02.280
that work at the
organization level.

00:36:02.280 --> 00:36:03.360
That's called OS log in.

00:36:03.360 --> 00:36:05.970
And if you're using
that, when you submit

00:36:05.970 --> 00:36:08.910
your SSH key, your public
key, to use the first time,

00:36:08.910 --> 00:36:11.100
you can also specify
the user name

00:36:11.100 --> 00:36:13.450
that should be used on
the instances there.

00:36:13.450 --> 00:36:16.390
And, of course, you're
logging into, usually,

00:36:16.390 --> 00:36:18.630
a Linux box, in
this case, for SSH.

00:36:18.630 --> 00:36:20.370
So you can use UNIX commands.

00:36:20.370 --> 00:36:23.760
And you can always pseudo
su into the user you

00:36:23.760 --> 00:36:26.218
want on the other end as well.

00:36:26.218 --> 00:36:27.010
JON FOUST: Awesome.

